        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, iron(II) chloride tetrahydrate (2.0 mmol, 0.20 g), sodium azide (4.0 mmol, 0.26 g), and N-methyldiethanolamine (Hmdea; 2.0 mmol, 0.238 g) were dissolved in acetonitrile/dichloromethane (10:10 mL). 3,5-Dinitrobenzoic acid (Hdnbz; 1.0 mmol, 0.21 g) and terbium(III) nitrate hexahydrate (0.5 mmol, 0.23 g) were added, giving a reddish solution. The mixture was stirred for 1 h, filtered, and left at room temperature. Red crystals formed within 3 days, were washed with acetonitrile, and dried in air.",
